# Styling Guide

This project uses [Tailwind CSS v4](https://tailwindcss.com) (via `@tailwindcss/vite`). All theme tokens live in [app.css](mdc:src/app.css). Style components with utility classes in markup; avoid `<style>` blocks unless something can't be expressed with utilities (e.g. `{@html}` content).

## Theme colors

Semantic colors follow the light/dark theme switch automatically:

| Utility suffix | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `fg-1`, `fg-2` | primary / secondary text |
| `surface-1` … `surface-4` | backgrounds, from base to most raised |
| `brand`, `brand-fg` | brand color and text on it |
| `link`, `link-visited`, `accent` | links and highlights |
| `star`, `planet`, `nebula` | space decorations |

```svelte
<div class="rounded-md border border-surface-3 bg-surface-2 p-5 text-fg-1">
	<a class="text-link hover:text-accent">Link</a>
	<span class="bg-brand/15">Translucent brand tint</span>
</div>
```

## Breakpoints

`xs` 360px, `sm` 480px, `md` 768px, `lg` 1024px, `xl` 1440px, `2xl` 1920px. Write mobile-first (`md:grid-cols-2`) or use `max-*` for "below" (`max-md:hidden`).

## Typography

- `.space-title`, `.space-subtitle`, `.space-heading` — page-level headings (responsive).
- `.prose` — wrapper for rendered markdown.

## Components

- Variant components (`Button`, `Badge`, `Link`, `Card`) use `cva` with Tailwind classes; merge consumer classes with `cn()` from `$lib/utils` so overrides win.
- Wrap pages in `OneColumnLayout`.
- Custom animations: `animate-twinkle`, `animate-ring-pulse`, `animate-placeholder-pulse` (set `[--pulse-min:…] [--pulse-max:…]`), `animate-gradient-shift`.
